{%- comment -%}
  Resolves a named spacing step to the design's own fluid value, and prints it.

  The merchant picks a step, not a number. A slider asks them to invent a
  figure and lets them pick 91 or 93 with no idea which is right; the theme
  then has to look correct at every one of fifty values. A step means the
  theme has to be right six times, and it means the same word is the same
  distance everywhere in the editor.

  The values are the reference design's own, carried over rather than
  re-derived. The design states section rhythm as an explicit
  clamp(min, vw, max) triple — a floor it holds on a phone, a slope it ramps
  on, and a ceiling it stops at. That is three decisions, and a single number
  cannot carry them: deriving the floor as a fixed fraction of the ceiling and
  the slope from (ceiling - floor) gives a different curve at every width,
  which is what this theme shipped before.

  The rungs are the design's own ceilings, deduplicated across its home,
  about, lookbook and footer pages — the ten it uses collapse to six within
  4px, and every rung below is a triple the design states verbatim somewhere:

    none    0
    2xs     30px                     Footer below — flat in the design, not a
                                     clamp: a 30px gap has nothing to gain by
                                     shrinking on a phone
    xs      clamp(40px, 5vw,  70px)  Footer above; Testimonials below
    sm      clamp(44px, 6vw,  84px)  Visit above; About pillars, About salon
    md      clamp(48px, 6vw,  90px)  The Craft; About craft band
    lg      clamp(56px, 7vw,  96px)  Our Products / Promises / About above;
                                     Find by Shape; Lookbook above
    xl      clamp(56px, 8vw, 110px)  Lookbook below; About salon below
    max     clamp(72px, 9vw, 120px)  Our Products / Promises / About below;
                                     Visit below

  Three of the design's own figures are not rungs and take the nearest:
  Most Loved's 72 and About's story 80 sit 2 and 4px off `xs` and `sm`, and
  Testimonials' 130 above is 10px over `max`. The footer's flat 30px below is
  not fluid at all and is left to that section — see Phase 4.

  A snippet cannot hand a value back to its caller, so this prints and the
  caller captures — the same shape as metal-order.liquid.

  Accepts:
    step  - one of the ids above. Anything unrecognised prints nothing, so the
            caller's own fallback stands rather than a broken value being
            emitted. Never print a bare keyword or `var(--step-)` here: both
            are invalid where a length is wanted, and an invalid value takes
            the whole declaration with it rather than falling back.

  Usage:
    {%- capture pad -%}{%- render 'space-step', step: 'lg' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- case step -%}
  {%- when 'none' -%}0px
  {%- when '2xs' -%}30px
  {%- when 'xs' -%}clamp(40px, 5vw, 70px)
  {%- when 'sm' -%}clamp(44px, 6vw, 84px)
  {%- when 'md' -%}clamp(48px, 6vw, 90px)
  {%- when 'lg' -%}clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px)
  {%- when 'xl' -%}clamp(56px, 8vw, 110px)
  {%- when 'max' -%}clamp(72px, 9vw, 120px)
{%- endcase -%}
